<title>NETHERLANDS: Salomon lifts Akzo Nobel EPS, price target.</title>
<headline>Salomon lifts Akzo Nobel EPS, price target.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Research note summary Aug 4</p>
<p>    Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>    Akzo Nobel	Chemicals     320.80  Salomon Bros</p>
<p>COMMENT: H1 results better than expected. We raise estimates about five pct. Company deserves sector P/E although tax rate will rise to more typical 35 percent in 2000. Stock had been limited by perception of poor management communication of strategy and reluctance to detail performance information. But improved format for results suggests management prepared to tackle issues. Stock can be re-rated to reflect underlying quality. We raise 12 month price target to NLG 360 from 300.</p>
<p>    Estimates (NLG):  EPS     pvs EPS   P/E    P/CF   Dividend</p>
<p>    1996 (actual)     18.50   -----     17.3   9.00    7.50</p>
<p>    1997		  21.80   20.60     14.7   8.00    8.20</p>
<p>    1998		  24.30   23.00     13.2   7.50    9.00</p>
<p>    1999		  27.40   26.00     11.7   6.90   10.00</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
